.TH STALLHUNT 1 "August 2026" "stallhunt 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stallhunt \- Linux performance triage that reports evidence-backed bottlenecks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stallhunt
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
.B stallhunt
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-details\fR | \fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B stallhunt hunt
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-details\fR | \fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B stallhunt watch
[\fB\-\-interval\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-count\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-plain\fR | \fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B stallhunt capabilities
[\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B stallhunt record
.B \-\-output
.I PATH
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDURATION\fR] [\fB\-\-redact\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR]
.PP
.B stallhunt replay
[\fB\-\-details\fR | \fB\-\-json\fR]
.I PATH
.PP
.B stallhunt redact
.I PATH
.B \-\-output
.I PATH
[\fB\-\-force\fR]
.PP
.B stallhunt completions
.I SHELL
.PP
.B stallhunt version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B stallhunt
observes a Linux host for a bounded interval, collects kernel telemetry, and
reports evidence-backed bottleneck findings for CPU scheduling, host memory,
block I/O, and bounded cgroup-v2 scope.
.PP
Running
.B stallhunt
with no subcommand is equivalent to
.BR "stallhunt hunt" .
Default human output is a compact resource summary with bounded ranked findings.
Use
.B \-\-details
for complete evidence, attribution, timing, and limitations.
Use
.B \-\-json
wherever supported to emit the full structured report.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B hunt
Run a bounded diagnosis over the requested observation window.
The default duration is 10 seconds.
.TP
.B watch
Track rolling finding lifecycle across repeated observation windows.
The default interval is 2 seconds.
With interactive input and output, watch opens a diagnosis-first TUI with
resource trends, finding navigation, selected attribution, and on-demand
explanation. Arrow keys or j/k select, Enter or d opens details, ? opens help,
and q quits cleanly. Redirected output and
.B \-\-plain
append compact windows. With
.BR \-\-json ,
one compact JSON object is printed per window.
Watch does not write recordings.
For an unlimited watch, the first SIGINT drains and writes the in-flight
window; a second SIGINT terminates immediately.
.TP
.B capabilities
Report which telemetry sources are available, partially available, unsupported,
permission denied, or failed on the current host.
.TP
.B record
Capture a normalized observation to a file for offline replay.
Requires
.BR \-\-output .
.TP
.B replay
Re-analyze a recording with the current inference engine without collecting live
telemetry.
.TP
.B redact
Replace identifiers in an existing recording and write a shareable copy.
.TP
.B completions \fISHELL\fR
Print shell completion scripts to standard output.
Supported shells:
.BR bash ,
.BR elvish ,
.BR fish ,
.BR powershell ,
and
.BR zsh .
.TP
.B version
Print the program name and version, then exit.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Duration and interval values
Options
.B \-\-duration
and
.B \-\-interval
accept values such as
.IR 500ms ,
.IR 2s ,
.IR 1.5s ,
and
.IR 1m .
The supported range is 100ms through 5m inclusive.
.SS Common options
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDURATION\fR
Observation duration for
.B hunt
and
.BR record .
Default:
.BR 10s " for both commands."
.TP
.BR \-\-interval " " \fIDURATION\fR
Rolling window size for
.BR watch .
Default:
.BR 2s .
.TP
.BR \-\-count " " \fIN\fR
Stop
.B watch
after
.I N
windows.
Omit to run until interrupted.
.I N
must be a positive integer.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON instead of human text.
Supported by
.BR hunt ,
.BR watch ,
.BR capabilities ,
and
.BR replay .
.TP
.B \-\-details
Render complete explanatory human text for
.B hunt
or
.BR replay .
Conflicts with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Force append-only human text for
.BR watch .
Conflicts with
.BR \-\-json .
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable color in human output. The
.B NO_COLOR
environment convention is also honored.
.TP
.BR \-\-output " " \fIPATH\fR
Output path for
.B record
or
.BR redact .
Required for both commands.
.TP
.B \-\-redact
When recording, replace process names, disk names, cgroup path components, and
inferred unit candidates before writing the file.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Overwrite an existing output file for
.B record
or
.BR redact .
By default, existing paths are not overwritten.
.SH OUTPUT
.SS Text
Human output summarizes findings, evidence, qualifiers, and timing.
The compact default bounds displayed findings and candidates; use
.B \-\-details
for the complete explanation.
Partial collection is reported explicitly rather than failing silently.
Sub-second hunts are telemetry smoke observations and do not receive healthy or
pressure verdicts.
.SS JSON
.B hunt
and
.B capabilities
emit versioned JSON reports with
.B schema_version
1.
.B watch \-\-json
emits one
.B stallhunt.watch_window
object per window.
.B replay \-\-json
re-renders the current inference result for a stored recording.
.SS Recordings
.B record
writes a normalized observation file with kind
.B stallhunt.recording
and
.B schema_version
1.
Recordings store analyzer input so
.B replay
can re-run current inference.
Hunt JSON is a report, not a recording, and is rejected by
.BR replay .
.B record
prints a short confirmation to standard output after a successful write.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure, including collection/render errors, unreadable recordings,
refused overwrites, or stdout write failures other than a broken pipe.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, including unknown commands/options and invalid argument values.
.TP
.B 130
An interactive or unlimited watch was aborted by a second SIGINT, or a bounded
interactive watch was interrupted.
.SH FILES
.SS Kernel and pseudo-filesystems read at runtime
.TP
.B /proc/pressure/cpu
Host CPU Pressure Stall Information.
.TP
.B /proc/pressure/memory
Host memory PSI.
.TP
.B /proc/pressure/io
Host block-I/O PSI.
.TP
.B /proc/stat
Host CPU counters.
.TP
.B /proc/loadavg
Runnable and uninterruptible queue context.
.TP
.B /proc/meminfo
Host memory occupancy and reclaim context.
.TP
.B /proc/vmstat
Host VM counters.
.TP
.B /proc/diskstats
Device-level I/O counters.
.TP
.B /proc/\fIPID\fR/stat
Process CPU, state, and identity.
.TP
.B /proc/\fIPID\fR/io
Process I/O counters when readable.
.TP
.B /proc/\fIPID\fR/task/\fITID\fR/schedstat
Task scheduler accounting when available.
.TP
.B cgroup2 mount
Unified cgroup-v2 hierarchy for bounded scoped context.
Per-cgroup PSI, controller counters, and membership are read only from
caller-visible groups under explicit collection limits.
.SS Recording files written by the tool
.TP
.B \fIPATH\fR
New recordings are created with mode
.B 0600 .
Existing paths are not overwritten unless
.B \-\-force
is supplied.
.SH RECORDING PRIVACY
Recordings may contain process names, cgroup paths, inferred systemd unit
candidates, device names, PIDs, start-time identities, and resource counters.
Treat recordings as potentially sensitive.
.PP
Default
.B record
retains identifiers for local diagnosis.
Use
.B record \-\-redact
or
.B redact
before sharing a copy.
Redaction replaces process names, disk names, cgroup path components, and
inferred unit candidates while keeping counters, PIDs, start times, major/minor
keys, and path hierarchy.
Redaction is not cryptographic anonymization.
.PP
Capture locally without redaction, then write a redacted copy before sharing.
.SH SUPPORT BASELINE
.TP
.B Platform
Linux with procfs mounted.
Readable PSI files under
.B /proc/pressure
are required for pressure verdicts.
Cgroup-v2 scoped context requires a unified cgroup2 mount visible to the
caller.
.TP
.B Privilege
Baseline collection is designed to run as an ordinary user.
Partial visibility is reported explicitly; the tool does not escalate
privilege by default.
.TP
.B Rust
Minimum supported Rust version (MSRV) is 1.85.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the default 10-second hunt:
.PP
.RS
stallhunt
.RE
.PP
Run a one-second hunt and emit JSON:
.PP
.RS
stallhunt hunt \-\-duration 1s \-\-json
.RE
.PP
Inspect available telemetry on the host:
.PP
.RS
stallhunt capabilities
.RE
.PP
Follow three rolling windows every two seconds:
.PP
.RS
stallhunt watch \-\-interval 2s \-\-count 3
.RE
.PP
Capture, replay, and redact a recording:
.PP
.RS
stallhunt record \-\-duration 10s \-\-output incident.json
.br
stallhunt replay incident.json
.br
stallhunt redact incident.json \-\-output incident.redacted.json
.RE
.PP
Install bash completions:
.PP
.RS
stallhunt completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash-completion/completions/stallhunt
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
Full project documentation is in the repository
.B docs/
directory.
.BR top (1),
.BR iostat (1),
.BR vmstat (1)
